# After a kernel is installed: the Sparky Stereo OS certificate, and this computer's DKMS certificate (DKMS's hook
# runs before this one and makes its key the first time it signs), stay next to every shim on the EFI system
# partition, so MokManager can enroll them from the disk (sparky-stereo-boot).
# The package was removed (this conffile stays until a purge): nothing to place.
[ -f /usr/lib/sparky-stereo-boot/secureboot.py ] || exit 0
# A certificate that cannot be placed is said here, in the system's language, and kept for repair by secureboot.py
# (sparky-stereo-boot status, and a notification at login). It does not stop the kernel's installation: this kernel
# boots without it, and a failing hook would keep zz-update-grub, which runs after this one (run-parts
# --exit-on-error in linux-run-hooks), from writing the new kernel's GRUB entry.
/usr/bin/python3 /usr/lib/sparky-stereo-boot/secureboot.py esp || :
exit 0
